  Read the margin column before concluding anything. At n = 53 the
  bio rule flags the cohort maximum whether it wins by 0.001 or 0.4,
  so the flag alone says nothing. The margin says whether the win
  was real. Where the margin is large AND the flags form a run of
  neighbouring CpGs, that is a focal epimutation and the per-sample
  summary is right for the wrong reason: it counts one event N times.
  Where the margin is small, the flag is noise.
